%% alt: The retrieval pipeline in detail. Indexing runs offline whenever sources change: parse and extract, chunk, enrich with metadata and context, then both embed and build a keyword index, stored together with permissions. Each query is rewritten or decomposed, runs keyword and vector search against the permission-filtered index, fuses the two result lists with reciprocal rank fusion, reranks, assembles context with citations, and generates the answer.
flowchart TB
  subgraph Ingest[Indexing, offline, on change]
    direction LR
    S[Sources]:::untrusted --> P[Parse, chunk]:::tool --> E[Enrich:<br/>metadata, context]:::tool --> V[Embed and<br/>keyword index]:::model --> I[(Index: vectors,<br/>text, permissions)]:::data
  end
  subgraph Query[Query, online, per request]
    direction LR
    T[Rewrite,<br/>decompose]:::model --> R[Keyword and<br/>vector search]:::tool --> F[Fuse RRF,<br/>rerank]:::model --> A[Context with<br/>citations]:::data --> G[Generate]:::model
  end
  Ingest -->|permission-filtered| Query
